g?fit=253%2C369&amp;ssl=1\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" class=\"size-medium wp-image-99 \" title=\"AKG C 547 BL\" alt=\"\" src=\"http:\/\/drumsandelectronics.files.wordpress.com\/2011\/09\/10-2.jpg?w=205&#038;resize=205%2C300\" width=\"205\" height=\"300\" srcset=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/10-2.jpg?w=253&amp;ssl=1 253w, https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/10-2.jpg?resize=206%2C300&amp;ssl=1 206w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 205px) 100vw, 205px\" data-recalc-dims=\"1\" \/><\/a><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-99\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">AKG C 547 BL<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n<p style=\"text-align: center\">I tested them with the same intent as I tested the <a title=\"Equipment standard\u00a0(preamp)\" href=\"http:\/\/drumsandelectronics.wordpress.com\/2011\/09\/13\/equipment-standard-preamp\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">preamps<\/a>, I wanted to see if there was any reason for me to invest in other microphones.<\/p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center\">I already have this one in all my drums:<\/p>\n<figure id=\"attachment_104\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-104\" style=\"width: 300px\" class=\"wp-caption aligncenter\"><a href=\"http:\/\/drumsandelectronics.files.wordpress.com\/2011\/09\/10-5.jpg\"><img data-attachment-id=\"104\" data-permalink=\"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/10-5\/\" data-orig-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/10-5.jpg?fit=1000%2C1000&amp;ssl=1\" data-orig-size=\"1000,1000\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-meta=\"{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}\" data-image-title=\"Ukko\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"&lt;p&gt;UKKO by b-band&lt;\/p&gt;\n\" data-medium-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/10-5.jpg?fit=300%2C300&amp;ssl=1\" data-large-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/10-5.jpg?fit=605%2C605&amp;ssl=1\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" class=\"size-medium wp-image-104 \" title=\"Ukko\" alt=\"\" src=\"http:\/\/drumsandelectronics.files.wordpress.com\/2011\/09\/10-5.jpg?w=300&#038;resize=300%2C300\" width=\"300\" height=\"300\" srcset=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/10-5.jpg?w=1000&amp;ssl=1 1000w, https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/10-5.jpg?resize=150%2C150&amp;ssl=1 150w, https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/10-5.jpg?resize=300%2C300&amp;ssl=1 300w, https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/10-5.jpg?resize=768%2C768&amp;ssl=1 768w, https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/10-5.jpg?resize=100%2C100&amp;ssl=1 100w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 300px) 100vw, 300px\" data-recalc-dims=\"1\" \/><\/a><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-104\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">UKKO by b-band<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n<p style=\"text-align: center\">Also I have three of these which I use for percussion (I apologize for the bad quality of the picture):<\/p>\n<figure id=\"attachment_113\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-113\" style=\"width: 300px\" class=\"wp-caption aligncenter\"><a href=\"http:\/\/drumsandelectronics.files.wordpress.com\/2011\/09\/10-6.jpg\"><img data-attachment-id=\"113\" data-permalink=\"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/10-6\/\" data-orig-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/10-6.jpg?fit=2592%2C1936&amp;ssl=1\" data-orig-size=\"2592,1936\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-meta=\"{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;2.8&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;iPhone 4&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;1316811424&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;3.85&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;1000&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0.066666666666667&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;6&quot;}\" data-image-title=\"Beyerdynamic TGX 5\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"&lt;p&gt;Beyerdynamic TGX 5&lt;\/p&gt;\n\" data-medium-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/10-6.jpg?fit=300%2C224&amp;ssl=1\" data-large-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/10-6.jpg?fit=605%2C452&amp;ssl=1\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" class=\"size-medium wp-image-113\" title=\"Beyerdynamic TGX 5\" alt=\"10-6\" src=\"http:\/\/drumsandelectronics.files.wordpress.com\/2011\/09\/10-6.jpg?w=300&#038;resize=300%2C224\" width=\"300\" height=\"224\" srcset=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/10-6.jpg?w=2592&amp;ssl=1 2592w, https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/10-6.jpg?resize=300%2C224&amp;ssl=1 300w, https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/10-6.jpg?resize=768%2C574&amp;ssl=1 768w, https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/10-6.jpg?resize=1024%2C765&amp;ssl=1 1024w, https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/10-6.jpg?w=1210&amp;ssl=1 1210w, https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/10-6.jpg?w=1815&amp;ssl=1 1815w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 300px) 100vw, 300px\" data-recalc-dims=\"1\" \/><\/a><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-113\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">Beyerdynamic TGX 5<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n<p style=\"text-align: center\">One of my main concerns regarding microphones when it comes to my setup is leakage, the amount of surrounding sounds that are picked up by the microphone <em>(Brice, 2001)<\/em>. The reason for this concern is that one of the techniques I use is based on amplitude-triggering: When the amplitude (volume) <em>(Knopp, 1996) <\/em>of a signal reaches a certain level, it generates a MIDI-signal<em><\/em>.<\/p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center\">I made a Max for Live patch for this:<\/p>\n<p><a href=\"http:\/\/drumsandelectronics.files.wordpress.com\/2011\/09\/10.png?resize=201%2C188\"><img data-attachment-id=\"86\" data-permalink=\"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/10\/\" data-orig-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/10.png?fit=201%2C188&amp;ssl=1\" data-orig-size=\"201,188\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-meta=\"{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}\" data-image-title=\"10\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-medium-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/10.png?fit=201%2C188&amp;ssl=1\" data-large-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/10.png?fit=201%2C188&amp;ssl=1\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" class=\"size-full wp-image-86 alignnone aligncenter\" title=\"10\" alt=\"audiotrigg\" src=\"http:\/\/drumsandelectronics.files.wordpress.com\/2011\/09\/10.png?resize=201%2C188\" width=\"201\" height=\"188\" data-recalc-dims=\"1\" \/><\/a><\/p>\n<p>If any one is interested in the .amxd-file or a standalone, please comment and I\u2019ll post it.<\/p>\n<p>The most suitable microphones for this concept are the built-in contact <a href=\"http:\/\/www.b-band.com\/ukko\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">microphones<\/a>. Since they are inside the drums they have a physical shield from their surroundings, and since they are contact microphones, sound waves in the air does not directly affect them. A contact microphone is\u00a0<em>&#8220;A microphone designed to pick up mechanical vibrations directly and convert them into corresponding electric currents or voltages&#8221; (McGraw-Hill Dictionary)<\/em>. Yet, I\u2019ve experienced that surrounding sound has made the drums resonate, and at high enough gain levels I\u2019ve experienced feedback. Still, compared to the other microphones I tried, they act very well when it comes to leakage, hear for your self:<\/p>\n<p>.<\/p>\n<p>Crown PZM 30 D (kick):<\/p>\n<iframe width=\"100%\" height=\"166\" scrolling=\"no\" frameborder=\"no\" src=\"https:\/\/w.soundcloud.com\/player\/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fapi.soundcloud.com%2Ftracks%2F23748940&width=false&height=false&auto_play=false&hide_related=false&visual=false&show_comments=false&color=false&show_user=false&show_reposts=false\"><\/iframe>\n<p>.<\/p>\n<p>AKG C 547 BL (kick):<\/p>\n<iframe width=\"100%\" height=\"166\" scrolling=\"no\" frameborder=\"no\" src=\"https:\/\/w.soundcloud.com\/player\/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fapi.soundcloud.com%2Ftracks%2F23748876&width=false&height=false&auto_play=false&hide_related=false&visual=false&show_comments=false&color=false&show_user=false&show_reposts=false\"><\/iframe>\n<p>.<\/p>\n<p>UKKO by b-band (snare):<\/p>\n<iframe width=\"100%\" height=\"166\" scrolling=\"no\" frameborder=\"no\" src=\"https:\/\/w.soundcloud.com\/player\/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fapi.soundcloud.com%2Ftracks%2F23748964&width=false&height=false&auto_play=false&hide_related=false&visual=false&show_comments=false&color=false&show_user=false&show_reposts=false\"><\/iframe>\n<p>.<\/p>\n<p>AKG C 518 (snare):<\/p>\n<iframe width=\"100%\" height=\"166\" scrolling=\"no\" frameborder=\"no\" src=\"https:\/\/w.soundcloud.com\/player\/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fapi.soundcloud.com%2Ftracks%2F23748844&width=false&height=false&auto_play=false&hide_related=false&visual=false&show_comments=false&color=false&show_user=false&show_reposts=false\"><\/iframe>\n<p>.<\/p>\n<p>Beyerdynamic TG-X 5 (snare):<\/p>\n<iframe width=\"100%\" height=\"166\" scrolling=\"no\" frameborder=\"no\" src=\"https:\/\/w.soundcloud.com\/player\/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fapi.soundcloud.com%2Ftracks%2F23748927&width=false&height=false&auto_play=false&hide_related=false&visual=false&show_comments=false&color=false&show_user=false&show_reposts=false\"><\/iframe>\n<p>.<\/p>\n<p>Unfortunately, the UKKO inside my kick isn&#8217;t working, they tend to not handle a lot of traveling, and I usually pack other drums inside the kick drum, so it might have been damaged for that reason.<\/p>\n<p>Since the kick microphones in question both are mounted inside the kick (many kicks have a hole in the rear drum head, so they are easy to mount), they don&#8217;t present the same amount of leakage as snare and tom microphones usually do.<\/p>\n<p>Even tough the UKKO&#8217;s present less leakage than the other microphones, they require you to always bring around drums with them mounted, or you&#8217;ll have to use some extra time mounting them in the drums where ever you go. Since there&#8217;s already so much equipment I have to bring around, and I&#8217;m looking for ways to minimize my setup, I don&#8217;t consider them as an option. There&#8217;s also the aspect of how they sound, we&#8217;ll look into that in the next post.<\/p>\n<p>I\u2019ve been looking into how to use other parameters as a input for the triggering, for example frequency or texture. If this method is thoroughly developed, I could in theory use just one overhead microphone and map the sound of each drum\/cymbal to a midi-note using for example this program: <a title=\"Wekinator\" href=\"http:\/\/wekinator.cs.princeton.edu\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Wekinator<\/a>. Then again, I would have to be alone on stage because other musicians could interfere with the triggering-system and it could present many challenges when I start looping or when it comes to feedback.<\/p>\n<p>Yet, this could be an interesting concept, multiple musicians interacting with one triggering system. For this, you would of course require a microphone with a lot of &#8220;leakage&#8221;.<\/p>\n<p>Next, we&#8217;ll look into the microphone setup.<\/p>\n<p>.<\/p>\n<p><em>Brice, Richard (2001),\u00a0Music Engineering, Oxford: Newnes,\u00a0ISBN\u00a00750650400<\/em><\/p>\n<p><em>Knopp, Konrad; Bagemihl, Frederick (1996).\u00a0Theory of Functions Parts I and II. Dover Publications. p.\u00a03.\u00a0ISBN\u00a00-486-69219-1<\/em><\/p>\n<p><em>McGraw-Hill Dictionary of Scientific &amp; Technical Terms, 6E, Copyright \u00a9 2003 by The McGraw-Hill Companies, Inc.<\/em><\/p>\n<div style=\"float: left;margin-right: 24px\"><a id=\"pd_a_5528639\"><\/a><div class=\"CSS_Poll PDS_Poll\" id=\"PDI_container5528639\" style=\"\"><\/div><div id=\"PD_superContainer\"><\/div><noscript><a href=\"https:\/\/polldaddy.com\/p\/5528639\" target=\"_blank\">Take Our Poll<\/a><\/noscript><\/div>\n<a id=\"pd_a_5528631\"><\/a><div class=\"CSS_Poll PDS_Poll\" id=\"PDI_container5528631\" style=\"\"><\/div><div id=\"PD_superContainer\"><\/div><noscript><a href=\"https:\/\/polldaddy.com\/p\/5528631\" target=\"_blank\">Take Our Poll<\/a><\/noscript>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>Lydrommet were also kind enough to lend me some microphones. I tested them with the same intent as I tested the preamps, I wanted to see if there was any rea